  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178066/assets/c89ac7325d47cb580e1479a90be32f923df0f17f8c478ad7265d135f4b1f4738.png)\n\nSolve for $x$ in the figure above given that $\\overset{⟷}{AB}∥\\overset{⟷}{CD}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the angles $∠FID$ and $∠IJB$ are corresponding angles, they are congruent and therefore have the same measure:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠FID & =m∠IJB \\\\ {60}^{∘} & =8x-{4}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have an equation that we can solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{60}^{∘} & =8x-{4}^{∘} \\\\ {64}^{∘} & =8x \\\\ \\frac{{64}^{∘}}{8} & =\\frac{8x}{8} \\\\ {8}^{∘} & =\\frac{\\cancel{8}x}{\\cancel{8}} \\\\ {8}^{∘} & =x \\\\ x & ={8}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
